          "line": 459,
          "message": "The new principal check covers only mocked IDs and does not catch the release identity receiving the existing subscription-scoped Contributor grant through the deployment input. Validate the effective input against the actual identity principals.",
          "confidence": 0.91,
          "category": "other",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The assertion compares terraform_principal_object_id only with the build and release principal IDs overridden to fixed mock values in this test run. The new C# check also compares the checked-in test fixture values, not the value supplied during a real Terraform apply.",
            "failureScenario": "If the deployment supplies terraform_principal_object_id equal to the release identity's actual principal ID, the existing subscription-scoped Contributor assignment grants that identity broad access. The mock IDs and configured test input remain different, so these checks pass. This leaves the previous AC RELEASE-ID-03 finding unresolved (OWASP A01:2025 Broken Access Control)."
          }
        }
